;; arbace.o2j from the checkout (bin/oi's o2j): the translator is embedded in the executables, and the tools' host loads a tool's
;; namespace from the checkout only under the prefixes RT.toolSource names (arbace/j2g/, arbace/repr/, ...), which arbace/o2j.ae is not
;; under: `-m arbace.o2j` ran the host's embedded copy, not the checkout's (found 2026-11-05, the compiled level's first changes). The
;; script loads the checkout's file (O2J_SRC, arbace/o2j.ae) and runs its -main with the command line:
;;
;;   EXE test/ocaml/o2j/tool.ae VERB ARG...
(load-file (System/getenv "O2J_SRC"))
(apply arbace.o2j/-main *command-line-args*)
